
  - [38;5;153msuccess: false[39m must not establish a session — no partial writes.
  - [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m returns [38;5;153mnull[39m when nobody is logged in; callers get a clear "unknown", never [38;5;153mundefined[39m.
  - [38;5;153msetSession[39m rejects a call with no userId rather than storing a broken record.
  - [38;5;153mclear()[39m exists from day one so logout has somewhere to go.

  [1m5. Security note (going into the spec, not up for design debate)[0m

  The stored userId is a client-side correlation value for "which form prefills for whom" and log readability. It is not
  proof of identity and must never gate access to anything. Any real authorization re-derives identity server-side from
  the session.

  [1m6. Two open decisions[0m

  [1mStub userId.[0m [38;5;153mlogin[39m never calls [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m — it returns a hardcoded success. So there is no real userId to derive
  yet. Either the stub synthesizes an obvious placeholder ([38;5;153m"stub-" + username[39m), which lets you wire and test the other
  forms immediately but puts fabricated identities into your logs, or it returns [38;5;153mnull[39m until real auth lands, which is
  honest but means [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m is null for every caller you build against in the meantime.

  [1mTesting.[0m The repo has no test runner, no linter, and no [38;5;153mscripts[39m in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m, so there's no established pattern to
  follow. Worth knowing: [38;5;153msession.js[39m as a browser IIFE isn't directly [38;5;153mrequire[39m-able, so Node-based tests need a few lines
  at the end of the file exporting it under [38;5;153mmodule.exports[39m when [38;5;153mmodule[39m exists. That's a small, common wart, but it is
  real added code.
